WEBVTT

00:00:00.363 --> 00:00:02.139
Last video ended with this question.

00:00:02.802 --> 00:00:05.045
Two hundred dollars goes into a super account

00:00:05.126 --> 00:00:06.608
at the end of every month for five

00:00:06.649 --> 00:00:08.812
years, earning a steady six per cent a

00:00:08.853 --> 00:00:10.575
year, compounded monthly.

00:00:11.157 --> 00:00:14.274
That's sixty deposits, twelve thousand dollars in total.

00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:17.349
Will the balance be exactly twelve thousand,

00:00:17.933 --> 00:00:18.474
a little more,

00:00:19.098 --> 00:00:19.941
or a lot more?

00:00:20.630 --> 00:00:21.058
Make a guess.

00:00:21.887 --> 00:00:24.073
You could run last video's rule sixty times,

00:00:24.435 --> 00:00:25.096
but that's slow.

00:00:25.659 --> 00:00:27.651
There's a faster way, if you follow each

00:00:27.692 --> 00:00:28.758
deposit on its own.

00:00:29.315 --> 00:00:31.022
Take the very last deposit.

00:00:31.566 --> 00:00:33.231
It goes in at the end of month

00:00:33.292 --> 00:00:35.640
sixty, and the balance is read straight away,

00:00:35.841 --> 00:00:37.165
so it earns no interest at all.

00:00:37.668 --> 00:00:38.954
It's worth two hundred dollars.

00:00:39.739 --> 00:00:41.759
The one before it has one month to

00:00:41.800 --> 00:00:44.541
grow, so it's two hundred times one point

00:00:44.582 --> 00:00:46.842
zero zero five, which is two hundred and

00:00:46.984 --> 00:00:47.423
one dollars.

00:00:48.268 --> 00:00:49.764
Now the very first deposit.

00:00:50.307 --> 00:00:51.994
It goes in at the end of month

00:00:52.216 --> 00:00:54.445
one, so it has fifty-nine months to grow.

00:00:54.988 --> 00:00:57.792
It's worth two hundred times one point zero

00:00:57.813 --> 00:01:00.798
zero five to the fifty-nine, about two hundred

00:01:00.819 --> 00:01:02.200
and sixty-eight dollars forty-three.

00:01:02.984 --> 00:01:05.190
Every deposit earns interest for a different length

00:01:05.232 --> 00:01:05.552
of time.

00:01:06.195 --> 00:01:09.126
So the future value is every deposit, together

00:01:09.167 --> 00:01:11.235
with the interest it has earned, all added

00:01:11.316 --> 00:01:11.395
up.

00:01:12.041 --> 00:01:13.556
Write them newest first.

00:01:14.419 --> 00:01:17.000
Two hundred, plus two hundred times one point

00:01:17.021 --> 00:01:17.901
zero zero five,

00:01:18.442 --> 00:01:20.783
plus two hundred times one point zero zero

00:01:20.824 --> 00:01:23.645
five squared, and so on, up to two

00:01:23.726 --> 00:01:26.147
hundred times one point zero zero five to

00:01:26.168 --> 00:01:26.867
the fifty-nine.

00:01:27.590 --> 00:01:28.714
That's sixty terms,

00:01:29.237 --> 00:01:30.180
one for each deposit.

00:01:30.783 --> 00:01:32.807
And each term is the one before it,

00:01:33.049 --> 00:01:34.672
times one point zero zero five.

00:01:35.350 --> 00:01:36.843
That's a geometric series.

00:01:37.369 --> 00:01:39.776
Its first term is two hundred, its ratio

00:01:39.937 --> 00:01:42.325
is one point zero zero five, and it

00:01:42.386 --> 00:01:43.428
has sixty terms.

00:01:44.051 --> 00:01:45.973
You already have its sum, from the sequences

00:01:46.014 --> 00:01:46.414
videos:

00:01:47.136 --> 00:01:49.278
a times r to the n, minus one,

00:01:49.439 --> 00:01:51.642
over r minus one, where r was the

00:01:51.703 --> 00:01:52.102
ratio.

00:01:52.785 --> 00:01:55.131
Here that's two hundred times one point zero

00:01:55.152 --> 00:01:58.159
zero five to the sixty, minus one, all

00:01:58.241 --> 00:02:00.165
over zero point zero zero five.

00:02:00.808 --> 00:02:04.202
That's thirteen thousand, nine hundred and fifty-four dollars

00:02:04.384 --> 00:02:05.106
and one cent.

00:02:06.011 --> 00:02:07.846
So it's a little more than twelve thousand.

00:02:08.471 --> 00:02:10.734
Five years isn't long, and the average deposit

00:02:10.775 --> 00:02:12.517
sits in the account for only about two

00:02:12.538 --> 00:02:14.601
and a half years, so the interest stays

00:02:14.722 --> 00:02:15.442
fairly small.

00:02:16.265 --> 00:02:18.873
On the statement, the extra one thousand, nine

00:02:18.935 --> 00:02:21.423
hundred and fifty-four dollars and one cent is

00:02:21.444 --> 00:02:22.045
the earnings.

00:02:22.621 --> 00:02:24.835
Does this agree with the month-by-month rule from

00:02:24.875 --> 00:02:25.458
last video?

00:02:26.243 --> 00:02:28.253
Use three deposits instead of sixty.

00:02:28.835 --> 00:02:31.080
The sum is two hundred times one point

00:02:31.140 --> 00:02:34.687
zero zero five cubed, minus one, over zero

00:02:34.707 --> 00:02:35.649
point zero zero five.

00:02:36.250 --> 00:02:38.192
That's six hundred and three dollars and one

00:02:38.272 --> 00:02:38.512
cent,

00:02:39.072 --> 00:02:41.534
exactly the balance the rule gave after three

00:02:41.574 --> 00:02:41.815
months.

00:02:42.577 --> 00:02:44.145
The rule adds month by month.

00:02:44.548 --> 00:02:46.628
The sum adds deposit by deposit.

00:02:47.071 --> 00:02:47.857
They're the same balance.

00:02:48.700 --> 00:02:50.821
In general, if M goes in at the

00:02:50.981 --> 00:02:53.342
end of each period, with interest at r

00:02:53.422 --> 00:02:55.884
per period, then the future value after n

00:02:56.344 --> 00:02:59.726
periods is M times one plus r to

00:02:59.766 --> 00:03:01.066
the n, minus one,

00:03:01.666 --> 00:03:02.367
all over r.

00:03:03.227 --> 00:03:05.389
The ratio of the series is one plus

00:03:05.629 --> 00:03:08.331
r, not r, so its bottom line, one

00:03:08.371 --> 00:03:10.512
plus r minus one, is just r.

00:03:11.476 --> 00:03:12.700
The formula has conditions.

00:03:13.284 --> 00:03:15.152
Payments come at the end of each period.

00:03:15.595 --> 00:03:17.102
The future value is read at the end

00:03:17.123 --> 00:03:19.412
of the last period, straight after the last

00:03:19.454 --> 00:03:19.794
payment.

00:03:20.418 --> 00:03:21.722
The account starts at zero,

00:03:22.446 --> 00:03:24.554
r is the rate per period, and n

00:03:24.735 --> 00:03:25.698
counts the periods.

00:03:26.403 --> 00:03:26.868
Let's use it.

00:03:27.791 --> 00:03:30.156
Three hundred dollars is deposited at the end

00:03:30.256 --> 00:03:32.280
of each month, at four point eight per

00:03:32.300 --> 00:03:34.124
cent a year, compounded monthly.

00:03:34.766 --> 00:03:36.773
What is the balance after five years?

00:03:37.618 --> 00:03:39.214
First match the period.

00:03:39.997 --> 00:03:42.563
The rate per month is zero point zero

00:03:42.623 --> 00:03:43.304
zero four,

00:03:43.825 --> 00:03:45.649
and five years is sixty months.

00:03:46.412 --> 00:03:49.055
So the future value is three hundred times

00:03:49.316 --> 00:03:51.378
one point zero zero four to the sixty,

00:03:51.719 --> 00:03:52.399
minus one,

00:03:52.961 --> 00:03:55.023
over zero point zero zero four.

00:03:55.645 --> 00:03:58.552
That's twenty thousand, two hundred and ninety-eight dollars

00:03:58.653 --> 00:03:59.414
and five cents.

00:04:00.156 --> 00:04:02.343
You put in eighteen thousand dollars, so the

00:04:02.404 --> 00:04:05.273
interest is two thousand, two hundred and ninety-eight

00:04:05.315 --> 00:04:06.438
dollars and five cents.

00:04:07.309 --> 00:04:09.880
Super runs for decades, so keep the same

00:04:09.921 --> 00:04:11.426
plan going for thirty years.

00:04:12.030 --> 00:04:14.052
You put in a hundred and eight thousand

00:04:14.093 --> 00:04:16.657
dollars, but the balance reaches two hundred and

00:04:16.798 --> 00:04:19.642
forty thousand, six hundred and forty-four dollars and

00:04:19.723 --> 00:04:20.463
twenty-four cents.

00:04:21.247 --> 00:04:21.772
Why so much?

00:04:22.458 --> 00:04:25.448
The early deposits have decades to grow, and

00:04:25.489 --> 00:04:27.837
the interest they earn starts earning interest too.

00:04:28.702 --> 00:04:30.632
Watch the gap between what you put in

00:04:30.894 --> 00:04:31.738
and what you have.

00:04:32.323 --> 00:04:33.839
It widens every year.

00:04:34.566 --> 00:04:37.539
After about twenty-six years, the interest has overtaken

00:04:37.741 --> 00:04:38.584
everything you put in.

00:04:39.336 --> 00:04:40.864
Here's a way to build the sum.

00:04:41.609 --> 00:04:43.076
Last in earns nothing.

00:04:43.580 --> 00:04:46.096
With a positive rate, first in earns the

00:04:46.137 --> 00:04:46.438
most.

00:04:47.242 --> 00:04:49.126
List the deposits from the last to the

00:04:49.227 --> 00:04:52.133
first, and each one is the one before,

00:04:52.214 --> 00:04:53.236
times one plus r.

00:04:54.179 --> 00:04:56.886
That's n terms, first term M,

00:04:57.408 --> 00:04:59.312
and ratio one plus r.

00:05:01.961 --> 00:05:02.390
Your turn.

00:05:02.959 --> 00:05:05.512
Write this future value as a sum, then

00:05:05.593 --> 00:05:05.934
find it.

00:05:06.580 --> 00:05:07.589
Pause here to answer.

00:05:18.336 --> 00:05:20.928
The last deposit earns nothing, and the first

00:05:21.029 --> 00:05:22.274
earns four years of interest.

00:05:22.858 --> 00:05:25.482
So the sum is nine hundred, plus nine

00:05:25.543 --> 00:05:27.266
hundred times one point zero five,

00:05:27.788 --> 00:05:30.051
up to nine hundred times one point zero

00:05:30.092 --> 00:05:30.973
five to the fourth.

00:05:31.756 --> 00:05:34.403
That's four thousand, nine hundred and seventy-three dollars

00:05:34.505 --> 00:05:35.266
and seven cents.

00:05:36.171 --> 00:05:38.265
Five thousand, two hundred and twenty-one dollars seventy-two

00:05:38.407 --> 00:05:38.870
is wrong.

00:05:39.133 --> 00:05:40.808
It pays every deposit at the start.

00:05:42.681 --> 00:05:43.088
Last one.

00:05:43.658 --> 00:05:46.246
Find the future value, and the interest earned.

00:05:46.709 --> 00:05:47.512
Pause here to answer.

00:05:58.168 --> 00:06:00.813
Monthly deposits need a monthly rate, zero point

00:06:00.855 --> 00:06:03.961
zero zero three, and n is twenty-four months.

00:06:04.483 --> 00:06:06.744
So the future value is six thousand, two

00:06:06.805 --> 00:06:09.967
hundred and eleven dollars sixty-three, and the interest

00:06:10.068 --> 00:06:12.049
is two hundred and eleven dollars sixty-three.

00:06:12.914 --> 00:06:14.480
Five hundred and nine dollars is wrong.

00:06:14.802 --> 00:06:16.963
It uses the yearly rate and two periods,

00:06:17.325 --> 00:06:19.046
and it's less than the deposits themselves.

00:06:20.787 --> 00:06:23.669
So a future value is a geometric sum,

00:06:24.090 --> 00:06:26.812
with one term for each payment and ratio

00:06:27.033 --> 00:06:27.873
one plus r.

00:06:28.636 --> 00:06:30.163
Back to three hundred dollars a month for

00:06:30.204 --> 00:06:32.194
five years, now in a savings app.

00:06:33.038 --> 00:06:34.639
What would make the biggest difference:

00:06:35.361 --> 00:06:37.142
a bigger deposit, a higher rate,

00:06:37.764 --> 00:06:38.383
more years,

00:06:38.885 --> 00:06:40.365
or some money in the account to start?

00:06:43.255 --> 00:06:44.138
Here are the key notes.

00:06:44.661 --> 00:06:46.429
Pause the video if you need more time

00:06:46.450 --> 00:06:46.931
to copy them.
